; EzyMap Scalp Mastery V2.2 BTC - EzyMap_V2_2_BTCUSD_RECOMMENDED.set
;
; ############################################################################
; #  NOT VALIDATED. NOT BACKTESTED. DO NOT TRADE THIS LIVE AS SHIPPED.       #
; #                                                                          #
; #  Every number below is a STRUCTURALLY REASONED starting point, not a     #
; #  tuned one. The build environment that produced this file had no MQL5    #
; #  toolchain and no BTC price history, so nothing here has been run        #
; #  through a single bar of data. Treat it as "the shape of a BTC config",  #
; #  and re-derive the magnitudes from your own broker's symbol before you   #
; #  risk money. V2_2_BTCUSD_CHANGES.md has a per-number retune checklist.   #
; ############################################################################
;
; Load this ON TOP of your V2.1b working set, on a BTCUSD or BTCUSD.sc chart.
; Every input not listed keeps its current value.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE ONE ASSUMPTION EVERYTHING ELSE HANGS OFF
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; StrategyPipSize() returns MathMax(1.0,_Point) for BTC, so ONE STRATEGY PIP
; ON BTC IS ONE US DOLLAR. On gold it is ten cents. Every "...Pips" input in
; this EA is therefore a DOLLAR AMOUNT on BTC and a DIME AMOUNT on gold.
;
; Gold M5 ATR(14) typically runs about $0.80-$1.50, i.e. 8-15 strategy pips.
; BTC M5 ATR(14) typically runs about $50-$150, i.e. 50-150 strategy pips.
; That is roughly an ORDER OF MAGNITUDE more pips for the same shape of move.
;
; So the working rule used throughout this file is: MULTIPLY GOLD'S FLAT PIP
; COUNTS BY 10. That preserves the RISK SHAPE (stop-to-ATR ratio, tolerance-
; to-ATR ratio, arm-to-stop ratio) rather than the absolute numbers, which is
; the only thing that can transfer between two instruments this different.
;
; ***  THE x10 IS THE ASSUMPTION MOST LIKELY TO BE WRONG.  ***
; BTC's volatility regime moves by a factor of 3-5 over a year in a way
; gold's does not. Read the actual figure off the OnInit log line
;   V2.2 BTC INSTRUMENT PROFILE ...
; and off RefreshGeometryATR()'s cached value, then rescale. If your BTC M5
; ATR is 30 pips rather than 100, everything below is roughly 3x too wide.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 1. ATR GEOMETRY - ON. This is the important one.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; V3.190 S03 is the correct lever for BTC precisely because it is SELF-
; RELATIVE: the stop is a multiple of the instrument's own current ATR, so it
; tracks a volatility regime shift automatically. The three MULTIPLIERS are
; dimensionless ratios and are deliberately LEFT AT GOLD'S TUNED VALUES -
; they encode the strategy's shape, not the instrument's scale.
;
; Only the FLOOR and CEILING are rescaled, because those three are the only
; ATR-geometry inputs denominated in pips (= dollars on BTC).
;   floor   12 -> 120   ceiling 35 -> 350   trail floor 5 -> 50
InpUseATRGeometry=true
InpATRPeriod=14
InpATRTimeframe=5
InpATRStopMultiplier=1.60
InpATRTrailMultiplier=0.55
InpATRArmMultiplier=0.35
InpATRStopFloorPips=120.0
InpATRStopCeilingPips=350.0
InpATRTrailFloorPips=50.0
;
; SANITY CHECK YOU MUST DO BEFORE RUNNING THIS:
; with M5 ATR = 100 pips, the resolved stop is 1.60*100 = 160, comfortably
; inside [120,350], which is what you want - the clamp should be a guard rail,
; not the operative value. If your ATR is 30, the stop wants to be 48 and the
; FLOOR of 120 overrides it, so every trade silently gets a 2.5x-too-wide
; stop and the sizing shrinks to match. If the floor or the ceiling is doing
; the work on most trades, the numbers are wrong. Check the log.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 2. STOP / TRAIL / BREAKEVEN PIP INPUTS
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; WITH InpUseATRGeometry=true, SOME OF THESE ARE OVERWRITTEN AT RUNTIME AND
; SOME ARE NOT. The exact trace is in V2_2_BTCUSD_CHANGES.md; the summary is:
;
;   FULLY SUPERSEDED (value replaced in ResolveATRGeometryPips):
;     InpPresetStopLossPips, InpTrailArmPips, InpTrailInitialDistancePips
;   PARTIALLY LIVE (rescaled by the ratio atrInitial/InpTrailInitialDistance-
;   Pips, so their RATIO to InpTrailInitialDistancePips still matters):
;     InpTrailTightDistancePips, InpTrailTightenAtPips
;   NEVER TOUCHED BY ATR GEOMETRY - these need real BTC tuning:
;     InpBreakevenLockAtPips, InpBreakevenLockOffsetPips,
;     InpTrailingActivationPips, InpPartialTPPips, all Grade*PartialTPPips,
;     all Distal* inputs, and every tolerance input in section 4
;
; The superseded ones are still set here because they are the LIVE VALUES
; whenever the ATR is unavailable (the first bars after attach, or a failed
; CopyBuffer), and because InpTrailInitialDistancePips is the shapeReference
; that produces the ratio applied to the two partially-live inputs.
InpPresetStopLossPips=210.0
InpTrailArmPips=70.0
InpTrailInitialDistancePips=70.0
InpTrailTightenAtPips=999.0
InpTrailTightDistancePips=70.0
InpTrailingActivationPips=0.0
InpTrailingDistancePips=70.0
InpTrailingStepPips=10.0
InpBreakevenLockAtPips=90.0
InpBreakevenLockOffsetPips=10.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 3. PARTIAL TP
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
InpPartialTPPips=110.0
InpGradeAPartialTPPips=160.0
InpGradeBPartialTPPips=110.0
InpGradeCPartialTPPips=70.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 4. TOLERANCES AND ZONE GEOMETRY - all live regardless of ATR geometry
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
InpEntryTouchTolerancePips=50.0
InpZeroConfTouchTolerancePips=90.0
InpZeroConfClusterTolerancePips=90.0
InpConfluenceTolerancePips=700.0
InpZoneIdentityTolerancePips=80.0
InpM1ZoneTolerancePips=80.0
InpSnrFrontRunPips=100.0
InpLimitZoneDuplicateTolerancePips=10.0
InpLiveLimitGeometryExtensionPips=200.0
InpTouchStallMaxExtendPips=20.0
;
; Mode stop/target scaffolding. These do NOT set the submitted SL (that comes
; from ResolvedPresetStopPips) - they feed the READY snapshot's RR planning
; and PersistentFallbackSL(), so they still have to be on the right scale.
InpScalpStopPips=200.0
InpIntradayStopPips=350.0
InpSwingStopPips=700.0
InpScalpTargetMinPoints=150.0
InpScalpTargetMaxPoints=800.0
InpIntradayTargetMinPoints=600.0
InpIntradayTargetMaxPoints=2500.0
InpSwingTargetMinPoints=1800.0
InpSwingTargetMaxPoints=8000.0
;
; Distal stops - only consumed when InpUseZoneDistalStops is true, which is
; NOT enabled here (leaving V2.0 S05 off is the V2.1b default). Set anyway so
; that turning it on later does not inherit gold's scale by accident.
InpDistalStopBufferPips=30.0
InpDistalStopMinPips=100.0
InpDistalStopMaxPips=300.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 5. ROUND-NUMBER GRADING (V2.0 S04, fixed by V2.2 BTC S01)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; V2.2 BTC S01 changed the checked levels on BTC from $5/$10 to $500/$1000.
; The tolerance has to move with them or the test flips from ALWAYS TRUE to
; almost never true. Gold: +/-$0.50 against a $5 grid = 20% of prices qualify.
; BTC: +/-$50 against a $500 grid = the same 20%. Shape preserved.
;
; Only consumed when InpUseZoneGrading is true; it is false by default and is
; NOT enabled here. Set so that enabling it later is not a trap.
InpRoundNumberTolerancePips=50.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 6. HIGHER-TIMEFRAME LEVEL SEPARATION FLOORS (new in V2.2 BTC S03)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The reason S03 exists. At gold's 70/120/200 these are $70/$120/$200 on BTC,
; which is inside a single M5 candle, so H4, D1 and W1 would all resolve onto
; effectively the same levels and the zero-conf ladder's whole W1 > D1 > H4
; priority ordering would be meaningless. x10 puts them at $700/$1200/$2000,
; i.e. roughly 0.7% / 1.2% / 2.0% of a $100k BTC - the same fraction-of-price
; those numbers represent on gold.
;
; JUDGMENT CALL: this is the input group I am least confident about, because
; the right answer depends on BTC's swing structure rather than on its ATR,
; and it interacts with the V2.1b S02 decision to trade only the OUTER W1/D1
; level. If the zero-conf ladder produces almost no W1 or D1 triggers, these
; are too wide. If W1/D1/H4 keep resolving to the same price, too narrow.
InpH4LevelMinDistancePips=700.0
InpD1LevelMinDistancePips=1200.0
InpW1LevelMinDistancePips=2000.0
InpH1LevelMinDistancePips=700.0
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 7. EXECUTION - SPREAD AND SLIPPAGE.  PLACEHOLDERS. VERIFY BEFORE USE.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; These two CANNOT be reasoned out from first principles, because the broker's
; point convention for BTCUSD is unknown at authoring time - BTC is variously
; quoted with 1, 2 or 3 digits, so "one point" can be $1, $0.01 or $0.001 and
; a spread of "1200 points" can mean $1200 or $1.20. Widened 10x from gold's
; 120/20 purely so a first attach does not reject every tick, WHICH IS NOT THE
; SAME AS BEING CORRECT.
;
; DO THIS FIRST: attach the EA and read the OnInit line
;   V2.2 BTC SPREAD CHECK | observed spread=... points (... price) | ...
; Watch it across a few minutes and across a session boundary, then set
; InpMaxSpreadPoints to roughly 2-3x the calm-market reading. BTC spreads
; widen far more violently than gold's around the CME open and at weekends.
InpMaxSpreadPoints=1200
InpDeviationPoints=200
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 8. MAGIC NUMBER - hygiene, not a bugfix
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Distinct from the XAUUSD default 2475176 so a BTC chart and a gold chart can
; run on the same account without ambiguity in the journal. Every position and
; order loop in this EA already double-filters on _Symbol AND InpMagicNumber,
; so the two would not actually interfere at the same magic - this is about
; being able to read the journal, not about correctness.
InpMagicNumber=2475222
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 9. SIZING - read the reasoning, the number is less obvious than it looks
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The intuition "BTC has a much bigger notional per lot, so size down hard" is
; usually WRONG for MT5 BTCUSD. A typical BTCUSD contract size is 1 BTC, so
; 1.00 lot at $100k is $100k notional. Gold's contract is 100 oz, so 1.00 lot
; at $3,300 is $330k notional - LARGER, not smaller.
;
; And because section 2 already scaled the stop by the same 10x as the pip,
; the DOLLAR RISK PER 0.01 LOT comes out almost identical:
;   gold : 21 pips  = $2.10 move, 0.01 lot = 1 oz    -> $2.10 risk
;   BTC  : 210 pips = $210 move,  0.01 lot = 0.01 BTC -> $2.10 risk
; So on RISK grounds the gold lot-per-100 ladder transfers unchanged.
;
; The real BTC constraint is MARGIN, not risk. Brokers commonly cap crypto
; leverage at 1:5-1:20 against 1:100-1:500 for gold, so the same 0.01 lot can
; tie up several times more margin. That is why the ladder is HALVED here
; rather than kept: it buys headroom so InpCentMaxMarginUsePct and
; CapVolumeForStandardRiskGuard are not clamping on every single deployment.
;
; IMPORTANT SCOPE NOTE: this ladder is only the TARGET. The final size is
; decided downstream by CapSetupVolumeForCentSafety() and
; CapVolumeForStandardRiskGuard(), which are broker-native - they call
; OrderCalcProfit and OrderCalcMargin against the real symbol - and will
; correct an over-sized target regardless of what is set here. So getting this
; wrong does NOT blow up the account's downside; it mostly determines how
; often the EA is pinned to the broker minimum lot (in which case the whole
; confidence/grade size ladder collapses into one flat size and every V2.0 S04
; grading result becomes untestable).
;
; VERIFY: if the log shows STANDARD RISK GUARD CAP or LIVE CENT MINIMUM-LOT
; CANDIDATE on most deployments, the ladder is mis-scaled for your account.
InpBaseEquity=100.0
InpBaseLayerLot=0.01
InpStandardSetupLotPer100=0.005
InpGoodSetupLotPer100=0.010
InpQualitySetupLotPer100=0.015
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 10. CONFLUENCE SCORING (V2.1a) - session OFF, volatility ON
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; JUDGMENT CALL, NOT A RULE.
;
; InpScoreSession is turned OFF for BTC. The V2.1a session model classifies
; the broker hour into OVERLAP / LONDON / NY / ASIA / DEAD, which encodes the
; FX-and-metals liquidity calendar. BTC trades 24/7/365 and has no London fix,
; no NY close and no weekend gap, so the DEAD bucket in particular would be
; penalising hours that are perfectly ordinary for crypto.
;
; This is NOT the claim that BTC has no hour-of-day structure - it demonstrably
; does, clustered around the CME open, the US cash session and the daily/weekly
; futures settlements. The claim is only that GOLD'S session map is the wrong
; map. The right move for a later iteration is to RE-TUNE the same mechanism
; against BTC's own observed hourly distribution (the four hour inputs and the
; four score inputs are all exposed, so this needs no code change at all) -
; not to conclude the mechanism does not apply. Disabling it here is the
; honest position while that data does not exist, not a finding.
;
; InpScoreVolatilityRegime STAYS AVAILABLE and is turned on: it percentile-
; ranks the current ATR against the instrument's OWN trailing distribution, so
; it is fully self-relative and transfers to BTC unchanged. On an instrument
; whose regime shifts as hard as BTC's, it is arguably worth more here than on
; gold.
;
; With session off, the aggregate score is just the volatility score, so
; InpMinConfluenceScore=0.45 admits normal (1.00) and rejects extreme (0.15).
; InpHardBlockExtremeVol is the separate outright veto and is left on.
;
; InpVolTimeframe=5 and InpVolATRPeriod=14 match InpATRTimeframe/InpATRPeriod
; above, so the V3.190 S03 geometry ATR handle is REUSED rather than a second
; one created. The init log states which handle was taken - check it.
InpUseConfluenceScoring=true
InpMinConfluenceScore=0.45
InpScoreSession=false
InpScoreVolatilityRegime=true
InpVolATRPeriod=14
InpVolTimeframe=5
InpVolPercentileLookback=500
InpVolLowPercentile=20.0
InpVolHighPercentile=90.0
InpVolatilityWeight=1.0
InpVolNormalScore=1.0
InpVolExtremeScore=0.15
InpHardBlockExtremeVol=true
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 11. WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT IN THIS FILE
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; InpUseZoneGrading, InpUseZoneDistalStops, InpUseV2RoutingChain,
; InpUseH1BiasFilter, InpZeroConfAllowCurrentMapTier, InpZeroConfIncludeLevel1
; and the whole V3.190 S01/S02/S04/S05 switch set are NOT set here. They are
; STRATEGY decisions that have to be A/B'd on BTC the same way they were on
; gold, one stage at a time, using the existing per-stage .set files. Bundling
; them into a "BTC config" would mean changing the instrument and six strategy
; switches in one step and learning nothing from the result.
;
; InpTreatSCSuffixAsCentOnLive is NOT set here either. Its default of true is
; already correct for BTCUSD.sc - ResolveAccountUnitDivisor()'s suffix test was
; never gold-gated - and V2.2 BTC S02 is what makes the PROTECTION side of
; that recognition finally engage on a BTC cent chart.
